sh at his belt) and the surgeon] [T-3594, the warrior's sash: a broad band wrapped round his hips in place of the rig's thin breechcloth, its top across the hips at y 293-298 and its foot sloping down to the west, from y 305 at his front to y 315 at his right hip, the fringed ends flying west out of it (the pouch); the cloth hanging from it at his right hip, in front of his stretched thigh, to its rounded foot at y 352 (x 488-505), and its fall beside the inner side of his raised thigh to y 350 (x 527-540), both where the plate draws them dark. The band stands a few pixels proud of the body's outline east of his hip, where the plate's tucks under Mrs. Helm's hand. Still to model: the faces themselves, and the surgeon's dress] [T-3594, the surgeon's pantaloons: in place of his rig's tight ones, loose heavy cloth on both legs from the hip past the knee to the boot's top, rumpled in creases and gathered over the boot, where the plate draws the leg he stretches west dark and thick from under Mrs. Helm's skirt to the boot (x 465-557, y 385-452, about 20 px through at the shin, as the render's now is). The render's leg runs 10-15 px lower than the plate's at the knee end, inside the pose's reading. Still to model: the faces themselves] [T-3594, the faces turned: Mrs. Helm's face, which looked straight out to the street over a level head, is turned to the warrior and bowed, as this plate draws her head in profile to the west with the brow, nose and chin at its lower left (x 575-590, y 222-242) and the knot of hair at its upper right (x 606-618, y 205-216); the render now draws the same profile, bowed about 30 degrees, the knot behind it. The child's face, which looked straight out, is lifted up and to the right after his hands, as his tilted head here (x 688-715, y 360-385) and Taylor's print show it. Still to model: the sculpted features of the faces themselves (the brows, noses and mouths the plate draws stronger than the rig's neutral face)]; behind the monument (contex